==============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY BIODIVERSITY DATA & MEDIA NOTICES
==============================================================================

The ANIMALIA software interfaces with external open-access biodiversity data
repositories. All third-party scientific data, photographs, and audio assets
remain the intellectual property of their respective creators and licensing
authorities:

1. Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF):
   Taxonomic backbone hierarchies and georeferenced specimen occurrence data
   are queried from the GBIF API (https://www.gbif.org) under Creative Commons
   CC-BY 4.0 and CC0 terms.

2. iNaturalist:
   Wildlife observational photography is queried via the iNaturalist API v1
   (https://www.inaturalist.org). Photographs remain copyrighted by their
   individual community observers and are displayed in ANIMALIA in accordance
   with their attributed Creative Commons licenses (CC0, CC-BY, CC-BY-SA,
   and CC-BY-NC).

3. Wikimedia Commons & Wikipedia:
   Natural history engravings, historical plates, and wildlife bioacoustic
   field recordings are sourced from Wikimedia Commons and Wikipedia under
   Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC-BY-SA 4.0), CC0, and Public
   Domain licenses.

4. IUCN Red List of Threatened Species:
   Conservation status categories and criteria codes are referenced from the
   IUCN Red List (https://www.iucnredlist.org) for scientific education and
   conservation awareness.
